-- EU AI Act, Chapter V: general-purpose AI models with systemic risk.
-- Articles 51 and 52 as far as they decide whether Article 55 applies to me,
-- the Article 52(1) notification clock, and Article 55(1)(c) on serious
-- incidents. Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 amends none of these provisions
-- (it replaces Article 56(6) only), so there is one vintage here.
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. See NOTES.md.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-domain`
IMPORT `aia-dates`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`

§ `Chapter V: general-purpose AI models with systemic risk`

§§ `Article 51: classification`

-- src:1309 | 2. A general-purpose AI model shall be presumed to have high impact capabilities pursuant to paragraph 1, point (a), when the cumulative amount of computation used for its training measured in floating point operations is greater than 1025.
-- src:1310 | 3. The Commission shall adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 to amend the thresholds listed in paragraphs 1 and 2 of this Article,
-- "1025" is the text file's flattening of 10 to the power 25; the Official
-- Journal XHTML has a superscript. See
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/eu-ai-act-2024-1689.formulas.md.
-- The exact literal is used: EXPONENT 10 25 is a floating-point value on the
-- main build and misses 10^25 by about 9 x 10^8.
-- Article 51(3) lets the Commission amend this threshold by delegated act.
-- No such act is deposited; the Regulation's own figure is used, and an
-- amendment would change the answers.
@ref Article 51(2) (src:1309); Article 51(3) (src:1310)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Article 51(2) threshold in floating point operations` MEANS 10_000_000_000_000_000_000_000_000

@ref Article 51(2) (src:1309)
GIVEN m IS A `model facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my model is presumed to have high impact capabilities` m MEANS
    m's `the cumulative training computation in floating point operations` GREATER THAN `the Article 51(2) threshold in floating point operations`

-- src:1304 | 1. A general-purpose AI model shall be classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk if it meets any of the following conditions:
-- src:1305 | (a)
-- src:1306 | it has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks;
-- src:1307 | (b)
-- src:1308 | based on a decision of the Commission, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel, it has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in point (a) having regard to the criteria set out in Annex XIII.
@ref Article 51(1)(a) (src:1304-1306); Article 51(2) (src:1309)
GIVEN m IS A `model facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my model meets the Article 51(1)(a) condition` m MEANS
        m's `an evaluation with appropriate technical tools found high impact capabilities`
    OR  `my model is presumed to have high impact capabilities` m

-- src:1315 | 3. Where the Commission concludes that the arguments submitted pursuant to paragraph 2 are not sufficiently substantiated and the relevant provider was not able to demonstrate that the general-purpose AI model does not present, due to its specific characteristics, systemic risks, it shall reject those arguments, and the general-purpose AI model shall be considered to be a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk.
-- Article 52(3) says only what follows a rejection. That an accepted
-- argument takes the model out of point (a) is read from Article 52(2)
-- ("should not be classified"): FORK F5. A Commission designation under
-- Article 51(1)(b) or 52(4) classifies the model whatever the arguments.
@ref Article 51(1) (src:1304-1308); Article 52(3) (src:1315)
GIVEN m IS A `model facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` m MEANS
        m's `it is a general-purpose AI model`
    AND (    (    `my model meets the Article 51(1)(a) condition` m
              AND (NOT (m's `the Commission has accepted my Article 52(2) arguments`)))
         OR m's `the Commission has designated it a model with systemic risk`)

§§ `Article 52(1): notifying the Commission`

-- src:1313 | 1. Where a general-purpose AI model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a), the relevant provider shall notify the Commission without delay and in any event within two weeks after that requirement is met or it becomes known that it will be met.
-- "Two weeks" is read as 14 calendar days; the day the condition is met, or
-- becomes known to be going to be met (whichever is earlier), is day 0.
@ref Article 52(1) (src:1313)
GIVEN m IS A `model facts`, `the date the condition was met or became known to be going to be met` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `deadline`
`by when must I notify the Commission under Article 52(1)` m `the date the condition was met or became known to be going to be met` MEANS
    IF     `I am the provider of the model` m
       AND m's `it is a general-purpose AI model`
       AND `my model meets the Article 51(1)(a) condition` m
    THEN `no later than` (`the date the condition was met or became known to be going to be met` PLUS 14)
    ELSE `no duty applies to me`

§§ `Article 55(1)(c): serious incidents`

-- src:1363 | 1. In addition to the obligations listed in Articles 53 and 54, providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk shall:
-- src:1368 | (c)
-- src:1369 | keep track of, document, and report, without undue delay, to the AI Office and, as appropriate, to national competent authorities, relevant information about serious incidents and possible corrective measures to address them;
-- "Serious incident" is defined in Article 3(49) as an incident or
-- malfunctioning of an AI system; the model's provider reports relevant
-- information about one. Article 55(1)(c) states NO number of days: the
-- answer is "no period stated", never Article 73's clocks.
@ref Article 55(1)(c) (src:1363) (src:1368-1369); Articles 111(3) and 113(b) as encoded in aia-dates.l4
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, m IS A `model facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`must I report the incident under Article 55(1)(c)` `the date` m i MEANS
        `I am the provider of the model` m
    AND `my model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` m
    AND `the date` AT LEAST `the date the Chapter V obligations bind me for this model` m
    AND `the incident is a serious incident` i

@ref Article 55(1)(c) (src:1368-1369)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, m IS A `model facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A `deadline`
`by when must I report under Article 55(1)(c)` `the date` m i MEANS
    IF `must I report the incident under Article 55(1)(c)` `the date` m i
    THEN `no period stated` "without undue delay"
    ELSE `no duty applies to me`

@ref Article 55(1)(c) (src:1368-1369)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, m IS A `model facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`
GIVETH A `recipient`
`to whom must I report under Article 55(1)(c)` `the date` m i MEANS
    IF `must I report the incident under Article 55(1)(c)` `the date` m i
    THEN `the AI Office and, as appropriate, national competent authorities`
    ELSE `no report is required of me`
